.TH sam-jail-gui 1 "2026-11-10" "SAM" "SAM - Sandboxed AppImage Manager"
.SH NAME
sam-jail-gui \- window of SAM \- Sandboxed AppImage Manager: sandbox AppImages and manage their permissions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sam-jail-gui
.RI [ APPIMAGE ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Opens SAM's window: the AppImages SAM found on the left, the selected app's
permissions, sandbox check and troubleshooting on the right. AppImages given
on the command line are added to the list. Starting it again brings the open
window forward and hands over the AppImages.
.PP
The window uses
.BR sam-jail (1)
for everything it does; the built-in user guide (menu \(-> User Guide)
explains every setting.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a short usage text.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME ", " XDG_DATA_HOME
Move the folders for SAM's settings, data and menu entries, as for other
programs.
.TP
.BR SAM_CONFIG_DIR ", " SAM_DATA_DIR ", " SAM_APPLICATIONS_DIR ", " SAM_RUNTIME_DIR
Use other folders for SAM's settings, data, menu entries and the files of
each start (testing).
Only developer builds of SAM read these variables; a release build keeps
its files in the standard folders.
.TP
.BR SAM_CLI ", " SAM_RUN
Use another
.B sam-jail
or
.B sam-jail-run
program. Only developer builds of SAM read these variables; a release
build takes SAM's programs next to it or, without them, a copy on
.B $PATH
that the user cannot change.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sam-jail (1),
.BR sam-jail-run (1)
